    {
      "id": "SWF-03",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "The spherical majorant in the strict convergence half-plane",
      "anchor": "lifts-siegel-weil-majorant",
      "statement": "For T=Re(s)+a/2>a, the positive spherical height powers are summable over the rational Siegel cosets. A label j∈ℕ^a contributes at most C^(1+T)(B^(a−T))^(Σj). This suffices for the convergence and holomorphy of the flat family in Re(s)>a/2.",
      "hypotheses": "The CM doubled Hermitian datum with nondegenerate form, compact Iwasawa subgroup and unitary Hecke character; cosets represented by rational group elements, with distinct cosets distinguished by their parabolic relation. The reduction supplies positive base B>1 and its height and counting bounds.",
